        "thought_text": "The previous approach using a greedy strategy may not be optimal for this problem, as it doesn't consider all possible combinations of colorings that could result in the desired beauty. Instead, a more effective approach would be to use dynamic programming to explore all possible valid colorings while keeping track of the minimum paint cost. This method ensures that we consider all possible ways to color the trees and find the one that results in the desired beauty with the least amount of paint.",
